Also an alternative way of working is to use a pre existant dataset to train a model, and then make our own dataset to test and fine tune the model, this was we start testing directly, and no need for collecting data to train a model
but to do this we have to follow the following procedures:

| **1. Develop using FEIS dataset** | Select two imagined speech sounds and build your preprocessing, feature extraction and classifier. Use only the imagined-speech portions. |
| **2. Collect EPOC X calibration data** | Have your participants imagine **the same two sounds**, with matching instructions and timing. |
| **3. Adapt the model** | Use part of your recordings to retrain or fine-tune it. Use separate validation recordings to select settings. |
| **4. Test independently** | Evaluate the final model on untouched recordings, preferably from another session. |
| **5. Demonstrate live control** | Process incoming EEG through the same pipeline and translate accepted predictions into device commands. |
